@startuml
title One request: the gate proxies, the UniversalNavigator drives the map

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam SequenceArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

actor Person
participant "Gate\n(facade)" as GATE
participant "UniversalNavigator\n(SharedServices)" as UN
participant "UtteranceManager" as UM
participant "Tool\n(local)" as LOC
participant "NavigatorProxy\n(satellite)" as PXY
participant "Tool\n(satellite)" as SAT
participant "Prose\n(own tool? or UM scope -- open)" as PROSE

Person -> GATE : session token, HTTP head,\nPOST/GET params  (each if present)
activate GATE
note over GATE #eef6f5
  The only component that knows transport exists.
  Collects, passes on, later writes the one stream.
  No routes of its own, no session check, no routing.
end note
GATE -> UN : token, head, params
activate UN

note over GATE, UN #fff7ed
  OPEN (REQ-B-001, handed to C6): the requirement text may place
  dispatch on the Gate. This design makes the Gate transport-only
  and the UniversalNavigator the sole dispatcher. Requirement is
  authoritative; the reconciliation is the operator's, not settled here.
end note

UN -> UN : session maintain / timeout / security\n(helper functions)
note right of UN #f3f4f6
  Session is validated here, not at the gate.
  Reads its env's live registry at startup and
  holds no data: the map is the registry,
  parameters ride the document, sessions and
  the ledger are repository rows.
end note

alt op is an utterance -- the person used words
  UN -> UM : the utterance  (no parameters)
  activate UM
  UM -> UM : preamble + every tool's fragment\n= one model call
  UM --> UN : the dispatch SET of routes\nnon-blocking, built for parallelism
  deactivate UM
  note right of UM #f3f4f6
    The classifier is gone -- this is it.
    Answers with routes; commands nothing.
  end note
else structured gesture -- the person worked a control
  UN -> UN : route straight from the map\nno model is asked
end

UN -> UN : validate the selection against may_call (a DAG);\ncompleteness: passed params vs prerequisites\n(a parameter/state conflict raises);\nrecord the render-ledger expectations;\nsign the dispatch out

par co-resident tool -- a direct function call
  UN -> LOC : dispatch (signed)
  activate LOC
  LOC -> LOC : work; may call another tool directly;\nre-raises on throw, never swallows
  LOC --> UN : internal callback (our signature)
  deactivate LOC
else satellite tool -- across the wire, via its proxy
  UN -> PXY : dispatch (signed) crosses the wire
  activate PXY
  PXY -> SAT : relay -- a local function call
  activate SAT
  SAT --> PXY : answer, or re-raised throw
  deactivate SAT
  PXY --> UN : internal callback (our signature)
  deactivate PXY
end

note over UN #eef6f5
  Serial deterministic merge via the shared library
  as each callback closes its ledger entry; the
  timeout facts race the callback; a conflict raises.
end note

UN -> PROSE : the facts to say
activate PROSE
PROSE --> UN : the user-facing sentence
deactivate PROSE
note over UM, PROSE #fff7ed
  OPEN ARCHITECTURAL QUESTION (not resolved here): is authoring the
  user-facing prose -- and asking the user a question -- the
  UtteranceManager's own scope, or a separate "Prose" tool?
  Drawn here as two participants only to show both halves; that
  layout is NOT a decision. Three approved requirements place prose
  and the manufacture path inside UtteranceManager
  (EPIC-002-F-010-S-001, -S-003, EPIC-006-F-008-S-003). The
  registry instance also carries a "Prose" route. Operator's to settle.
end note

UN --> GATE : sequenced events, one at a time
deactivate UN
GATE -> Person : the one stream\n(the gate that opened it writes it)
deactivate GATE
@enduml
